{{also|coïncide|coïncidé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-}}
From {{bor|en|fr|coïncider}}, from {{der|en|ML.|[[coincido|coincidere]]}}, from {{m|la|con-}} + {{m|la|[[incido|incidere]]}}, from {{af|la|in-|id1=in|t1=into, to|[[cado|cadere]]|gloss2=to fall, fall down, drop}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-coincide.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪd}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|intransitive}}

# To occupy exactly the same [[space]].
#: {{ux|en|The two squares '''coincide''' nicely.}}
# To occur at the same time.
#: {{ux|en|The conference will '''coincide''' with his vacation.}}
# To [[correspond]], [[concur]], or [[agree]].
#: {{ux|en|Our ideas '''coincide''', except in certain areas.}}

